<section image-layout="blank" id="8sfUyJLQAY" background-overlay="tint" background-overlay-intensity="0.28"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/4hhnrIPSHSO_nUqv6hIKz.png" saved-media-id="aei2xyadekhgkvw" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="secure-stack-isometric" alt="Matte isometric 3D software infrastructure, a single luminous cyan request packet travelling toward a translucent browser portal and a violet security gate on the right, dark graphite server blocks and a database cylinder receding behind them, controlled cyan and violet rim light, deep near-black negative space across the left half, crisp shadows, no text, no lettering, no people" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1920,&quot;height&quot;:1088}"><freeform><box type="content" x="48" y="52" w="585" h="414" sizing="fixed" background-color="rgba(9,17,31,0.84)" style="padding: 28pt 30pt; border: 1pt solid rgba(88, 230, 255, 0.22); border-radius: 12pt;"><p role="eyebrow">B.Tech · Node.js laboratory</p><h1 font-size="40pt">Student Authentication Portal:<br>what happens between “Log in” and “Welcome, Priya”</h1><p font-size="lg">A proposed reference implementation traced from password storage to a verified profile request.</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><p font-size="sm">Register · Log in · Profile · Logout</p></box><box type="content" x="684" y="218" w="214" h="78" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="padding: 12pt 14pt; border-radius: 10pt;"><p role="eyebrow" align="center">Request in flight</p><p align="center"><code>POST /api/auth/login</code></p></box></freeform></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="sqGgrQPmhZ"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="q-QP3J9zEo"><h2>Fast hashes fail after a breach—start at the database</h2><p>Plaintext and <code>SHA-256(password)</code> both fail after a breach: offline attackers can test guesses at full speed.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="g5jp12GT7E" cell-style="subtle" padding="0" colspan="26"><grid direction="vertical" spacing="none"><grid-item id="VdJfVNyUPj" background-color="surface" row-size="auto" padding="8pt 14pt"><p font-size="sm"><code>localhost:27017 · students</code></p></grid-item><grid-item id="WgKYFiZz3K" row-size="fill" padding="12pt 14pt"><h3>What a stolen table reveals</h3><table col-widths="[24,49,27]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="--table-cell-padding: 5pt 7pt;"><tbody><tr><td><p>Method</p></td><td><p>Stored field</p></td><td><p>Verdict</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Plaintext</p></td><td><p><code>college@123</code></p></td><td><p>Exposed</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>SHA-256</p></td><td><p><code>sha256(password)</code></p></td><td><p>Too fast</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>bcrypt</p></td><td><p>Salted, adaptive hash</p></td><td><p>Lab choice</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p font-size="sm">The database breach is the threat model: the server is no longer available to slow guesses down.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="OKYDBoTrms" cell-style="subtle" padding="10pt 12pt" colspan="34"><table col-widths="[28,72]" header-row="true" header-col="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="--table-cell-padding: 5pt 7pt;"><tbody><tr><td><p>Security principle</p></td><td><p>Practical consequence</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="14pt">Speed is the attack</p></td><td><p font-size="14pt">Fast hashes permit huge guess volumes; password hashing must be deliberately expensive.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="14pt">Salt defeats lookup tables</p></td><td><p font-size="14pt">A unique salt makes two copies of <code>college@123</code> produce different stored values, defeating precomputed rainbow tables.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="14pt">Recommendation vs. lab</p></td><td><p font-size="14pt">OWASP prefers Argon2id: 19 MiB, 2 iterations, parallelism 1. Legacy bcrypt uses work factor ≥10 and has a 72-byte limit. This lab uses cost 12 for portability and readable output.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p role="caption">Source: <a href="https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Password_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html">OWASP Password Storage Cheat Sheet</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="LSDy6Onagg"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="nKET-xUAYs"><h2>Three tiers, one trust boundary, and everything interesting happens at the middle one</h2><p>No application code ships with this deck. This is the proposed reference implementation for the lab build.</p><freeform-block w="840" h="300"><box type="image" w="840" h="300" src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/9qLYVd7swBLo2yfxCwsju.png"></box><shape preset="line" x="282" y="18" w="2" h="264" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="3"></shape><shape preset="rightArrow" x="234" y="130" w="88" h="28" fill="accent" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="rightArrow" x="519" y="130" w="88" h="28" fill="accent" stroke-width="0"></shape><box type="content" x="239" y="8" w="90"><p role="eyebrow" align="center">Trust boundary</p></box><box type="content" x="22" y="52" w="214" h="208" sizing="fixed" background-color="rgba(9,17,31,0.88)" style="padding: 16pt; border: 1pt solid rgba(88, 230, 255, 0.28); border-radius: 11pt;"><labels><label variant="solid">Client</label></labels><h3>Browser</h3><p>HTML/CSS and <code>fetch()</code> with <code>credentials: "include"</code>. Two forms and a profile page.</p><p font-size="sm">Holds no authority. Cannot read the token.</p></box><box type="content" x="316" y="38" w="214" h="234" sizing="fixed" background-color="rgba(16,27,48,0.94)" style="padding: 16pt; border: 2pt solid rgba(155, 123, 255, 0.68); border-radius: 11pt;"><labels><label variant="solid">API</label></labels><h3>Node.js + Express</h3><p><code>/register</code> · <code>/login</code><br><code>/profile</code> · <code>/logout</code></p><p font-size="sm">bcryptjs · jsonwebtoken · cookie-parser · dotenv · <a href="https://github.com/express-rate-limit/express-rate-limit/blob/main/readme.md">express-rate-limit</a></p></box><box type="content" x="604" y="52" w="214" h="208" sizing="fixed" background-color="rgba(9,17,31,0.88)" style="padding: 16pt; border: 1pt solid rgba(89, 242, 195, 0.3); border-radius: 11pt;"><labels><label variant="solid">Data</label></labels><h3>MongoDB + Mongoose</h3><p><code>Student</code> stores roll number, email and <code>hash</code>.</p><p font-size="sm">Plaintext password is never a field, never logged and never returned.</p></box><box type="content" x="236" y="166" w="84"><p font-size="sm" align="center">request + cookie</p></box><box type="content" x="521" y="166" w="84"><p font-size="sm" align="center">query + result</p></box></freeform-block></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="nLHZIX1mfL"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="oE0O1A7uJH"><h2>Registration: bcrypt stores salt, cost &amp; algorithm</h2><p><code>POST /api/auth/register</code>. Validate, reject duplicates, hash, and store. The demo moment is one 60-character database field containing every parameter.</p><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="XQK8J43lR-" background-color="palette-2" text-color="#09111F" padding="10pt 12pt" colspan="10"><p role="eyebrow">Variant</p><h4><code>$2b$</code></h4><p font-size="sm">bcrypt variant</p></grid-item><grid-item id="a1msvR62kK" background-color="accent" padding="10pt 12pt" colspan="10"><p role="eyebrow">Cost</p><h4><code>12$</code></h4><p font-size="sm">+1 doubles the work</p></grid-item><grid-item id="E7Cbi1gH1o" background-color="surface" padding="10pt 12pt" colspan="20"><p role="eyebrow">Salt · 22 characters</p><h4><code>Xy7…</code></h4><p font-size="sm">Unique per stored password</p></grid-item><grid-item id="PuLM6UkQ9b" background-color="surface" padding="10pt 12pt" colspan="20"><p role="eyebrow">Digest · 31 characters</p><h4><code>…</code></h4><p font-size="sm">Result of the expensive hash</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="Qzs_fBif8A" cell-style="subtle" padding="0" colspan="38"><grid direction="vertical" spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="FnuOnbmUmL" background-color="surface" padding="7pt 12pt"><p font-size="sm"><code>auth.controller.js</code></p></grid-item><grid-item id="Z-ULrlp4Wb" padding="10pt 12pt"><pre language="javascript"><code>const hash = await bcrypt.hash(req.body.password, 12)
await Student.create({ rollNo, email, hash })</code></pre><p font-size="sm">No salt column: the bcrypt string contains the variant, cost, salt, and digest.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="5tsQE6-X72" colspan="22"><table col-widths="[7,17]" header-col="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="--table-cell-padding: 8pt 10pt;"><tbody><tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>Request</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm"><code>POST /api/auth/register</code><br><code>rollNo</code> · <code>email</code> · <code>password</code></p></td></tr><tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>201</b><br>Created</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Return the student’s name and roll number. <b>Never return the hash.</b></p></td></tr></tbody></table><p font-size="sm">bcrypt format reference: <a href="https://passlib.readthedocs.io/en/stable/lib/passlib.hash.bcrypt.html">Passlib documentation</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="DvklozH_k3"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="UJDgnGys-U"><h2>Login: compare, sign, set an HttpOnly cookie</h2><p><code>bcrypt.compare</code> re-hashes the submitted password with the stored salt; success signs a 15-minute JWT and sets it as an HttpOnly cookie.</p><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="hx4u9y61w_" background-color="surface" padding="10pt 16pt"><p font-size="12pt"><code>const token = jwt.sign({ sub: student._id, role: "student" }, process.env.JWT_SECRET, { expiresIn: "15m" })</code><br><code>res.cookie("token", token, { httpOnly: true, secure: true, sameSite: "strict", maxAge: 900000 })</code></p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="11pt">JWT: three parts / two dots; encoded and signed, not encrypted. <code>secure: true</code> needs HTTPS; the lab flag is environment-driven. Structure: <a href="https://auth0.com/docs/secure/tokens/json-web-tokens/json-web-token-structure">Auth0</a>.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="uKhlN1R_Ny" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">JWT anatomy</p><grid direction="vertical" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="1P5S_KCWcw" background-color="accent" padding="6pt 12pt"><p><b>Header · </b><code><span text-color="#F5F8FF"><b>header</b></span></code><br><span font-size="13pt">Algorithm metadata.</span></p></grid-item><grid-item id="-vdUgsc7dp" background-color="palette-2" text-color="#09111F" padding="6pt 12pt"><p><b>Payload · </b><code><span text-color="#F5F8FF"><b>{ sub, role, exp }</b></span></code><br><span font-size="12pt">Base64Url JSON; not encrypted. Exclude marks, fees and personal data.</span></p></grid-item><grid-item id="8AKyoHn9JS" background-color="palette-3" padding="6pt 12pt"><p><b>Signature · </b><code><span text-color="#F5F8FF"><b>signature</b></span></code><br><span font-size="13pt">Proves the server minted the token and its claims were not edited.</span></p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="sMVai17169" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Login outcomes</p><grid direction="vertical" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="AbqsLHQ7Z9" cell-style="subtle" padding="6pt 12pt"><p><b>Request · </b><code><b>POST /api/auth/login</b></code><br><span font-size="13pt">The browser submits the email and password.</span></p></grid-item><grid-item id="3nocyfnyz6" cell-style="subtle" padding="6pt 12pt"><p><b>200 · Authenticated · Set-Cookie</b><br><code><span font-size="11pt">token=&lt;JWT&gt;; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict; Max-Age=900</span></code></p></grid-item><grid-item id="ScAxASh7JC" cell-style="subtle" padding="6pt 12pt"><p><b>401 · Invalid credentials</b><br><span font-size="13pt">Unknown email and wrong password use the same message.</span></p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="usXE-zC_Ex"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Wz95_x1VH3"><h2>Authorization lives in about 12 lines of middleware</h2><p><code>GET /api/student/profile</code> never sees an unverified request. The guard attaches an identity or ends the request.</p><freeform-block w="840" h="184"><shape preset="rightArrow" x="150" y="47" w="32" h="20" fill="accent" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="rightArrow" x="350" y="47" w="32" h="20" fill="accent" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="rightArrow" x="594" y="47" w="32" h="20" fill="accent" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="line" x="267" y="100" w="2" h="38" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="2"></shape><shape preset="line" x="489" y="112" w="2" h="26" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="2"></shape><shape preset="line" x="735" y="100" w="2" h="38" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="2"></shape><box type="content" y="14" w="148" h="86" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 8pt; border-radius: 10pt;"><p role="eyebrow" align="center">Request</p><h4 align="center">Cookie arrives</h4><p font-size="sm" align="center"><code>token</code></p></box><box type="content" x="188" y="14" w="160" h="86" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 8pt; border-radius: 10pt;"><p role="eyebrow" align="center">Read</p><h4 align="center"><code>cookie-parser</code></h4><p font-size="sm" align="center"><code>req.cookies.token</code></p></box><box type="content" x="388" y="2" w="204" h="110" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 8pt 10pt; border: 2pt solid rgb(155, 123, 255); border-radius: 12pt;"><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/UcRBDyidoaD0u4QxPaiV.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="security shield signature verification gate"></icon><h4 align="center">Verify gate</h4><p font-size="sm" align="center"><code>jwt.verify(token,</code><br><code>process.env.JWT_SECRET)</code></p></box><box type="content" x="632" y="14" w="208" h="86" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 8pt; border-radius: 10pt;"><p role="eyebrow" align="center">Attach</p><h4 font-size="16pt" align="center"><code>req.user = payload</code></h4><p font-size="sm" align="center"><code>next()</code></p></box><box type="content" x="188" y="140" w="160" h="38" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="rgba(155,123,255,0.18)" style="padding: 6pt; border: 1pt solid rgba(155, 123, 255, 0.62); border-radius: 8pt;"><p font-size="12pt" align="center"><b>401</b> · no cookie</p></box><box type="content" x="392" y="140" w="196" h="38" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="rgba(155,123,255,0.18)" style="padding: 6pt; border: 1pt solid rgba(155, 123, 255, 0.62); border-radius: 8pt;"><p font-size="12pt" align="center"><b>401</b> · tampered or expired</p></box><box type="content" x="634" y="140" w="202" h="38" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="rgba(155,123,255,0.18)" style="padding: 6pt; border: 1pt solid rgba(155, 123, 255, 0.62); border-radius: 8pt;"><p font-size="12pt" align="center"><b>403</b> · valid, insufficient role</p></box></freeform-block><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="T5P0YBGcBu" cell-style="subtle" padding="12pt 14pt" colspan="20"><h4>Pin the algorithm</h4><p font-size="sm">Verify the signature and <code>exp</code>; fix the expected algorithm so <code>alg: none</code> is rejected.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="5YCetoZ8tj" cell-style="subtle" padding="12pt 14pt" colspan="20"><h4>Cookie means CSRF duty</h4><p font-size="sm">Use <code>SameSite=strict</code> as defence in depth; state-changing routes still need a CSRF token.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="lW6CgQKZqv" cell-style="subtle" padding="12pt 14pt" colspan="20"><h4>Live test</h4><p font-size="sm">Edit one cookie character in DevTools. The same profile request becomes a 401.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">CSRF references: <a href="https://owasp.org/www-community/SameSite">OWASP SameSite</a> and the <a href="https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross-Site_Request_Forgery_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html">OWASP CSRF Prevention Cheat Sheet</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="ygxivTqcVi"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="U0WQDVKVRj"><p role="eyebrow">LIVE TEST CONSOLE · FOUR VIVA DECISIONS + ONE HONEST GAP</p><h2>Logout, expiry &amp; the revocation limit</h2><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="FZhg_tC0zz" colspan="38"><table col-widths="[24,55,21]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="--table-cell-padding: 3pt 7pt;"><tbody><tr><td><p>Check</p></td><td><p>Reference implementation</p></td><td><p>Observed</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Cookie, not localStorage</p></td><td><p><code>httpOnly</code>, <code>Secure</code>, <code>SameSite=strict</code>. JS cannot read the cookie; XSS can still defeat CSRF.</p></td><td><labels><label variant="solid">Contained</label></labels></td></tr><tr><td><p>Secret handling</p></td><td><p><code>.env</code> gitignored; <code>.env.example</code> committed; no secret literal in <code>app.js</code>.</p></td><td><labels><label variant="solid">PASS</label></labels></td></tr><tr><td><p>Login rate limit</p></td><td><p><code>express-rate-limit</code>: per-IP attempt cap in fixed <code>windowMs</code>.</p></td><td><labels><label variant="outline">429</label></labels></td></tr><tr><td><p>Logout</p></td><td><p><code>POST /api/auth/logout</code> calls <code>res.clearCookie("token")</code> with matching attributes.</p></td><td><labels><label variant="solid">Cleared</label></labels></td></tr></tbody></table><p font-size="sm">References: <a href="https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross-Site_Request_Forgery_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html">OWASP CSRF guidance</a> · <a href="https://github.com/express-rate-limit/express-rate-limit/blob/main/readme.md">express-rate-limit</a>.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="0BikfD1cnh" background-color="palette-2" text-color="#09111F" colspan="22"><labels><label variant="outline">Unresolved limit</label></labels><display size="md">15m</display><h3>The revocation gap remains</h3><p>A signed token remains valid until <code>exp</code>; a copy taken before logout can verify for the rest of the 15-minute lifetime.</p><hr thickness="sm"><p>Close it with short-lived access tokens plus refresh rotation, or a <code>jti</code> denylist checked per request. Either restores server-side state.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>